          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            = succeed "," do
              %strong exponentiable functor
            %strong Conduché functor
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %strong Conduché fibration
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            which is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponentiable+morphism"} exponentiable morphism
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stigler%27s+law+of+eponymy"} Stigler's law of eponymy
            %a{:href => "#Giraud64"} Giraud 64
            before
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#Conduche72"} Conduché 72
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibrations"} Grothendieck fibrations
            and opfibrations.
          %p
            So, roughly speaking, a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon E\to B
            is a
            %strong strict Conduché functor
            if given any morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
          %h2#failure_of_local_cartesian_closedness_in_cat Failure of local cartesian closedness in Cat
          %p
            As is evident from the fact that such functors have a name, not every functor is exponentiable in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+category"} locally cartesian closed
          %p
            It is easy to write down examples of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            that are not preserved by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            (as they would be if pullback had a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
            denote the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/walking+arrow"} walking arrow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal"} ordinal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            regarded as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} terminal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 3
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mn 1
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{3} = \mathbf{2} \sqcup_1 \mathbf{2}
            the ordinal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 3
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi b
                  %mo →
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3 = (a \to b \to c)
            regarded as a category. Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            square
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mn 2
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{1 &amp; \overset{}{\to} &amp; \mathbf{2}\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                  \\mathbf{2}&amp; \underset{}{\to} &amp; \mathbf{3}}
          %p
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat/\mathbf{3}
            pulls back along the inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}\to \mathbf{3}
            of the arrow
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a\to c)
            to the square
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                          %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{0 &amp; \overset{}{\to} &amp; 1\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                  1&amp; \underset{}{\to} &amp; \mathbf{2}}
          %p which is certainly not a pushout.
          %p
            One way to describe the problem is that the pushout has “created new morphisms” that didn’t exist before. But another way to describe the problem is that the inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}\to\mathbf{3}
            fails to notice that the morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a\to c)
            acquires a new factorization in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{3}
            which it didn’t have in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon E\to B
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %strong strict Conduché functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha\colon a\to b
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            and any factorization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mi a
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi β
                  %mi c
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi γ
                  %mi p
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p a \overset{\beta}{\to} c \overset{\gamma}{\to} p b
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \alpha
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                there exists a factorization
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mover
                          %mi β
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi d
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mover
                          %mi γ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \overset{\tilde{\beta}}{\to} d \overset{\tilde{\gamma}}{\to} b
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mover
                        %mi β
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo =
                      %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \tilde{\beta} = \beta
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mover
                          %mi γ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mo =
                        %mi γ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \tilde{\gamma} = \gamma
            %li
              %p
                any two such factorizations in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                are connected by a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zigzag"} zigzag
                of commuting morphisms which map to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_c
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            (Here, ‘commuting morphism’ means a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo →
                  %mi d
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \to d'
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            such that the pair of triangles in
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi d
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mover
                              %mi γ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mtd
                          %mi b
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mover
                                %mi β
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↗
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mover
                                  %mi γ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                %mo ′
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi a
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mover
                                %mi β
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                              %mo ′
                        %mtd
                          %mi d
                          %mo ′
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp; &amp; d &amp; \stackrel{\tilde{\gamma}}{\to} &amp; b \\
                  \&amp; ^\mathllap{\tilde{\beta}} \nearrow &amp; \downarrow &amp; \nearrow^\mathrlap{\tilde{\gamma}'} &amp; \\
                  a &amp; \underset{\tilde{\beta}'}{\to} &amp; d' &amp; &amp;
                  }
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"}> commute
            \.)
          %p The theorem is then that the following are equivalent:
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is a strict Conduché functor.
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponentiable+morphism"} exponentiable
              in the 1-category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is exponentiable in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"} strict 2-category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cat
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
          %p
            By “exponentiable in the strict 2-category
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            has a strict right 2-adjoint (i.e. a
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotensors"} cotensors
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
          %p
            For exponentiability in the weak
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon E\to B
            is a
            %strong (weak) Conduché functor
            if for any morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha\colon a\to b
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            and any factorization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mi a
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi β
                  %mi c
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi γ
                  %mi p
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p a \overset{\beta}{\to} c \overset{\gamma}{\to} p b
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \alpha
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                there exists a factorization
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mover
                          %mi β
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi d
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mover
                          %mi γ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \overset{\tilde{\beta}}{\to} d \overset{\tilde{\gamma}}{\to} b
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mi d
                        %mo ≅
                        %mi c
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p d \cong c
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mover
                        %mi β
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo =
                      %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \tilde{\beta} = \beta
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mover
                          %mi γ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mo =
                        %mi γ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \tilde{\gamma} = \gamma
            %li
              %p
                any two such factorizations in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                are connected by a zigzag of commuting morphisms which map to isomorphisms in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            A functor can then be shown to be a weak Conduché functor if and only if it is exponentiable in the weak sense in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
          %p
            A Conduché functor is
            %strong discrete
            if each factorisation is unique (equivalently, if it reflects identities). Discrete Conduché functors generalise
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+fibrations"} discrete fibrations
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+opfibrations"} discrete opfibrations
          %p
            Discrete Conduché functors are said to satisfy the
            = succeed "." do
              %strong unique lifting of factorisations
            %strong ULF
            functors.
          %h3#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              ULF functors form the right class of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+factorisation+system"} orthogonal factorisation system
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
          %h2#conduch_functors_and_2functors_to_prof Conduché functors and 2-functors to Prof
          %p
            The Conduché criterion can be reformulated in a more conceptual way by analogy with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibrations"} Grothendieck fibrations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon E\to B
            is essentially the same as to give a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+lax+functor"} normal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+2-functor"} lax 2-functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi Prof
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to Prof
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Prof"} Prof
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctors"} profunctors
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/displayed+category"} displayed category
          %p
            Specifically, given a functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi Prof
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to Prof
            as follows. Each object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in B
            is sent to the fiber category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{-1}(b)
            of objects lying over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            and morphism lying over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_b
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon a\to b
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            to the profunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi ⇸
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_f\colon p^{-1}(a) &amp;#8696; p^{-1}(b)
            for which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_f(x,y)
            is the set of arrows
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\to y
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            lying over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi f
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi g
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_f \otimes H_g \to H_{g f}
            are given by composition in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            from a normal lax 2-functor into
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Prof
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prof
            is an evident generalization of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is a fibration iff the corresponding functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi Prof
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to Prof
              factors through a pseudo 2-functor landing in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Cat
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat^{op}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Cat
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %mi Prof
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat^{op}\to Prof
            %li
              Similarly,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is an opfibration iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi Prof
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to Prof
              factors through a pseudo 2-functor landing in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
              via the covariant inclusion
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cat
                      %mo →
                      %mi Prof
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat \to Prof
            %li
              The functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi Prof
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to Prof
              factors through a
              %em lax
              2-functor landing in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Cat
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat^{op}
              iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              admits all “weakly cartesian” liftings, and dually.
            %li
              Finally,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is a (strict) Conduché functor iff the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi Prof
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to Prof
              is itself a pseudo 2-functor (though it may not land in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
              or
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Cat
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat^{op}
          %p
            Thus Conduché functors into
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            correspond to pseudofunctors from
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Prof
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prof
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            do not correspond to pseudonatural transformations between such pseudofunctors. To get the correct transformations, we must instead regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            as a vertically discrete
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+category"} double category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Prof
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prof
            as a pseudo double category with profunctors horizontally and functors vertically; then pseudo double functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi Prof
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to Prof
            again correspond to Conduché functors into
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %em vertical
            double transformations between them correspond to functors between Conduché functors into
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            More generally, the slice category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat/B
            is equivalent to the hom-category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Dbl
                      %mrow
                        %mi normal
                        %mo ,
                        %mi lax
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Prof
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Dbl_{normal,lax}(B,Prof)
          %h2#highercategorical_versions Higher-categorical versions
          %p
            Non-strict Conduché functors and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Street+fibrations"} Street fibrations
            may be equivalently characterized by an “up-to-iso” version of the above constructions using
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+fibers"} essential fibers
          %p
            %a{:href => "#AyalaFrancis"} Ayala and Francis
            prove an analogous characterization of exponentiable
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} (∞,1)-functors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-categorical context
            eliminates the “level-shifting” in the characterization via
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Prof
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prof
            (i.e. the presence of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Prof"} Prof
            when discussing only exponentiable 1-functors). Thus, there is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29Prof"} (∞,1)Prof
            such that exponentiable
            = succeed "-functors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            correspond to
            = succeed "-functors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Prof
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to (\infty,1)Prof
          %p
            As in the 1-categorical case, ordinary
            = succeed "-transformations" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Prof
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to (\infty,1)Prof
            do not give the correct maps between exponentiable
            = succeed "-functors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Prof
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)Prof
            as a sort of “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            \-double category”. Ayala and Francis consider only the vertically-invertible fragment of this
            = succeed "-double" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proarrow+equipment"} proarrow equipment
            with all 2-cells and all 1-cells in the domain invertible); this is what they call a “flagged”
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+space"} Segal space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Prof
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)Prof
            also restricts what it classifies to the
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-functors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            rather than the whole
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %h2#in_a_double_category__completeness In a double category - completeness
          %p
            Functors satisfying a Conduché-like condition are central to completeness/cocompleteness in
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                pseudo-double categories
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/pseudo-double+categories"} ?
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is complete iff for any small
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            and locally small
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo :
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K: M\to C
            a functor,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T : A\to M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            has a pointwise right Kan extension along
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo :
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K: M\to C
            satisfying a Conduché condition.
          %p
            A pseudo-double category is
            %em unitary
            if the vertical identity arrows are strict identities, so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi A
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi f
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_A\circ f = f = f\circ 1_B
            on-the-nose. We here assume all double categories are unitary; this is not a severe restriction in practice.
          %p
            Call a lax functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝔸
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔹
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: \mathbb{A}\to\mathbb{B}
            between pseudo-double categories
            %em unitary
            if it it preserves identity vertical arrows on-the-nose and the comparison map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi FA
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_{FA}\to F(1_A)
            is the identity; therefore it is only really lax from the point of view of composition. A unitary lax functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔸
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\to\mathbb{A}
            is automatically strict, as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            has no nontrivial compositions, whereas a lax functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔸
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\to\mathbb{A}
            is an object endowed with a vertical monad.
          %p
            Note that if we are working in a 2-category of lax functors, and we want to define the limit of a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝔸
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔹
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : \mathbb{A}\to\mathbb{B}
            as the right Kan extension of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            along
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo !
                      %mi 𝔸
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} !_{\mathbb{A}}:\mathbb{A}\to 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔹
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\to \mathbb{B}
            along unitary lax functors rather than lax functors, so that our answer is just an object of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔹
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{B}
            and a cocone rather than a vertical monad in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔹
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{B}
          %p
            The correct definition of “complete” for a pseudo-double category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔸
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}
            is that it admits pointwise unitary lax right Kan extensions of any lax double functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝕀
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔸
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S: \mathbb{I}\to\mathbb{A}
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕀
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
            small) along all lax double functor along a lax double functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝕀
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝕁
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R: \mathbb{I}\to\mathbb{J}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            satisfies the “right Conduché condition: that the laxity 2-cell for vertical composition in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %div{:style => "text-align: center"}
